<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Clement XIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1693–1769</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clement XIII, born Carlo Rezzonico in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, was pope from 1758 to 1769. His pontificate was dominated by the defence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> against the Catholic monarchies, which expelled them from Portugal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and Parma. His Monitorium of 1768 against the church reforms of the Duchy of Parma led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> courts to occupy papal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-clement-xiii.jpg" alt="Pope Clement XIII" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Raphael Mengs · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton_Raphael_Mengs_-_Portrait_of_pope_Clement_XIII,_c._1760.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
